"comparison": "Both JPMorgan and Bank of America define the Supplementary Leverage Ratio (SLR) using the same regulatory framework components: Tier 1 capital as the numerator and total leverage exposure as the denominator. Both explicitly state the minimum requirement of 3.0% for Basel III Advanced approach organizations and the additional 2.0% leverage buffer required for systemic firms. JPMorgan defines total leverage exposure as average on-balance sheet assets (net of deductions) plus off-balance sheet exposures. Bank of America aligns on the numerator (quarter-end Basel 3 Tier 1 capital) and denominator structure (daily average on-balance sheet exposures less deductions and average off-balance sheet exposures), confirming the identical calculation methodology and regulatory minima.",
